image.prompt:
Create an image with the following specification.

Subject: {subject}
Position: {subject_position}
Scale: {subject_scale}
Spatial layout: {spatial}
Scene: {scene}
Shot: {shot_type}
Camera angle: {camera_angle}
Style: {style}
Lighting: {lighting}
Color: {color}
Composition: {composition}
Camera: {photo_params}
Material: {material}
Quality: {quality_words}
Text in image: {text_content}
References: {reference_note}
Constraints: render all text exactly as written; no extra text, logos, or watermarks. {negative_words}

image.recreate:
Recreate the referenced image as faithfully as possible.

Subject: {subject}
Position: {subject_position}
Scale: {subject_scale}
Spatial layout: {spatial}
Shot: {shot_type}
Camera angle: {camera_angle}
Lighting: {lighting}
Color: {color}
Material: {material}
Style: {style}
Preserve: {preserve_constraints}
Avoid: {forbidden_changes}
Do not invent details that are not visible in the reference; do not restyle the image.

image.edit:
Edit the provided image.

Change: {target_style}
Modification scope: {modification_scope}
Preserve unchanged: {preserve_constraints}
Do not change: {forbidden_changes}
Keep all other content, composition, lighting, color and existing text exactly as is.

image.reference_guided:
Create an image using the provided references.

Reference roles:
{reference_images}

Subject: {subject}
Spatial layout: {spatial}
Style: {style}
Lighting: {lighting}
Color: {color}
Composition: {composition}
Material: {material}
Constraints: use each reference only for its assigned role; do not transfer unlisted attributes. {negative_words}

image.compose:
Compose a new image from the provided references.

Element sources:
{reference_images}

Placement: {subject_position}
Scale: {subject_scale}
Spatial layout: {spatial}
Style: {style}
Lighting: {lighting}
Color: {color}
Composition: {composition}
Constraints: match perspective, light direction, color temperature and material across all elements; do not simply collage the references.
